# Revisions to skip when running git blame - whitespace-only, no content changed.
#
# Use with:  git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
# (per-clone; .git/config is not committed). Entries must be FULL 40-char SHAs;
# git rejects an abbreviation with "fatal: invalid object name".
#
# NOTE for the line-ending commit below: this file does NOT hide it. git can only
# reassign a line it can still match in the parent, and a CRLF->LF rewrite changes
# every line, so blame keeps attributing them to the rewrite. Use `git blame -w`
# instead, which ignores the trailing CR and finds the real author:
#
#     git blame -w CHANGELOG.md      # -> c71af746 (2018), the actual author
#     git blame    CHANGELOG.md      # -> the renormalisation
#
# The entry is kept because it is correct in intent and will work for ordinary
# reformatting commits added later, where lines remain matchable.

